---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import Showcase from "../../../components/Showcase.astro";

const html = `<section
  class="sk-box"
  data-surface="raised"
  data-border="subtle"
  data-padding="lg"
>
  <h3>Summary</h3>
  <p>A semantic section with surface, edge and padding.</p>
  <button type="button">Administrar</button>
</section>`;

const react = `import { Box } from "@skryensya/react/box";

<Box as="section" surface="raised" border="subtle" padding="lg">
  <h2>Summary</h2>
  <p>The content preserves the semantics of the chosen element.</p>
  <button type="button">Administrar</button>
</Box>;`;
---
<Base title="Box" description="Visual and semantic surface chosen by the user; without own interaction.">
  <h1>Box</h1>
  <p class="lede">Box only has surface, edge and padding. Whoever uses it chooses the semantic element. It does not provide interaction or convert the content into a destination or action.</p>

  <h2>When to use it</h2>
  <p>Use Box for static content or for a surface with several independent controls. If the entire surface represents exactly one interaction, choose the corresponding semantic component: <a href="/en/components/link">Link</a>, <a href="/en/components/button">Button</a>, <a href="/en/components/checkbox">Checkbox</a>, <a href="/en/components/radio-group">RadioGroup</a> or <a href="/en/components/accordion">Accordion</a>.</p>
  <p>Box and Tile share surface, border, radius, and the <code>padding</code> vocabulary. Use <code>data-padding="none"</code> in HTML or <code>padding="none"</code> in React when the header or content image must touch the border; That child declares its own inset. The difference between the two is exclusively the interaction that Tile does have.</p>
  <p>The <a href="/en/components/card">Card</a> guide applies this decision to content, news, product, link, action, selection and metrics cards.</p>

  <h2>HTML autorado</h2>
  <Showcase html={html} react={react} label="Box" />

  <h2>React</h2>
  <p>The code is in the <strong>React</strong> tab of the preview.</p>

  <h2>Contrato</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>In HTML, choose the semantic element and add the <code>sk-box</code> class.</li>
    <li><code>data-surface</code> acepta <code>none</code>, <code>sunken</code>, <code>surface</code> o <code>raised</code>.</li>
    <li><code>data-border</code> acepta <code>none</code>, <code>subtle</code> o <code>default</code>.</li>
    <li><code>data-padding</code> acepta <code>none</code>, <code>xs</code>, <code>sm</code>, <code>md</code>, <code>lg</code> o <code>xl</code>.</li>
    <li>In React, <code>as</code> selects the element; <code>surface</code>, <code>border</code> and <code>padding</code> render those attributes.</li>
  </ul>
</Base>
